collationcmds.c: a domain does not run "locale -a" (intcap plan, Phase D).

initdb's --single call imports the system collations with pg_import_system_collations,
which popen()s "locale -a". A domain cannot spawn a process, so the call failed ("could
not execute command "locale -a": No file descriptors available") after 356 setup
statements. Under Capstone, READ_LOCALE_A_OUTPUT is not defined, as on a platform
without "locale -a": no libc collations are imported. pg_collation therefore lacks the
rows a native initdb adds, which a comparison with native output has to allow for.

--- a/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
+++ b/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
@@ -579,7 +579,9 @@
 
 
 /* will we use "locale -a" in pg_import_system_collations? */
-#if !defined(WIN32)
+/* capstone: not in a domain, which cannot spawn a process; initdb then imports
+ * no libc collations, as on a platform without "locale -a". */
+#if !defined(WIN32) && !defined(__SIZEOF_INTCAP__)
 #define READ_LOCALE_A_OUTPUT
 #endif
 
